d.
It is understood and agreed that these policies are primary and not contributory. All
policies required under this agreement shall be in effect for the duration of the project and
agreement.  Insurance certificates must include a clause stating that the insurance may not
be canceled, amended or allowed to lapse until the expiration of at least thirty (30) days
advance written notice to the City of Cheyenne.

e.
The City of Cheyenne shall be named as an additional insured on the Company's
insurance policies, except workers' compensation, and the Company shall provide a copy
of the endorsement providing this coverage.

f.
The City has the right to reject a certificate of insurance if the Company's insurance
company is widely regarded in the insurance industry as financially unstable.  Any
insurance company providing coverage under this contract shall have a minimum A.M.
Best rating of A- (excellent).

g.
The City has the right to review the certificates of any or all subcontractors used by the
Company. Further, the City requires that the subcontractors' insurance coverage be
equivalent to that required of the Company.

h.
The City has the right to increase the required minimum limit of liability on the
agreement as warranted by an increase in hazard.  Examples of increased hazard include,
but are not limited to:

1.  handling of hazardous materials
2.  activities involving large congregations of people

i.
